{"term":"patrol","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:50a2f48e93f21c5488","definition":"A going of the rounds along the chain of sentinels and between the posts, by a guard, usually consisting of three or four men, to insure greater security from attacks on the outposts.","example":"Four members of the squadron were on patrol.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["border patrol","combat air patrol","dawn patrol","donut patrol","emu patrol","foot patrol","highway patrol","long-range reconnaissance patrol","military patrol","nonpatrol","on eternal patrol","patrol boat","patrol bomber","patrol cap","patrol car","patrol leader","patrolman","patrol officer","patrolperson","patrol ship","patrol van","patrol vehicle","patrol wagon","patrolwoman","saturation patrol","senior patrol leader","Sharia patrol","shore patrol","ski patrol","squadrol"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patrol#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e67a838155d9e80433","definition":"A movement, by a small body of troops beyond the line of outposts, to explore the country and gain intelligence of the enemy's whereabouts.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["border patrol","combat air patrol","dawn patrol","donut patrol","emu patrol","foot patrol","highway patrol","long-range reconnaissance patrol","military patrol","nonpatrol","on eternal patrol","patrol boat","patrol bomber","patrol cap","patrol car","patrol leader","patrolman","patrol officer","patrolperson","patrol ship","patrol van","patrol vehicle","patrol wagon","patrolwoman","saturation patrol","senior patrol leader","Sharia patrol","shore patrol","ski patrol","squadrol"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patrol#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6d3dac97fdcc4d6d98","definition":"The guards who go the rounds for observation; a detachment whose duty it is to patrol.","example":"After cordial good-bye to our hospitable hostess we motored back to Chaumont where we dined with Colonel Mitchell; and then with another long drive we finally reached home tired but happy at 3.30 in the morning. There staring me in the face was an order directing me to lead my patrol over the lines in the morning at five o'clock, sharp! An hour and a half sleep for an utterly worn out aviator!","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["border patrol","combat air patrol","dawn patrol","donut patrol","emu patrol","foot patrol","highway patrol","long-range reconnaissance patrol","military patrol","nonpatrol","on eternal patrol","patrol boat","patrol bomber","patrol cap","patrol car","patrol leader","patrolman","patrol officer","patrolperson","patrol ship","patrol van","patrol vehicle","patrol wagon","patrolwoman","saturation patrol","senior patrol leader","Sharia patrol","shore patrol","ski patrol","squadrol"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patrol#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3216a9b771481123fc","definition":"The largest division of officers within a police department or sheriff's office, whose assignment is to patrol and respond to calls for service.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["border patrol","combat air patrol","dawn patrol","donut patrol","emu patrol","foot patrol","highway patrol","long-range reconnaissance patrol","military patrol","nonpatrol","on eternal patrol","patrol boat","patrol bomber","patrol cap","patrol car","patrol leader",