 was ready.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["border patrol","combat air patrol","dawn patrol","donut patrol","emu patrol","foot patrol","highway patrol","long-range reconnaissance patrol","military patrol","nonpatrol","on eternal patrol","patrol boat","patrol bomber","patrol cap","patrol car","patrol leader","patrolman","patrol officer","patrolperson","patrol ship","patrol van","patrol vehicle","patrol wagon","patrolwoman","saturation patrol","senior patrol leader","Sharia patrol","shore patrol","ski patrol","squadrol"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patrol#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4b28013fa9a2f1c77e","definition":"To go the rounds along a chain of sentinels; to traverse a police district or beat.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["border patrol","combat air patrol","dawn patrol","donut patrol","emu patrol","foot patrol","highway patrol","long-range reconnaissance patrol","military patrol","nonpatrol","on eternal patrol","patrol boat","patrol bomber","patrol cap","patrol car","patrol leader","patrolman","patrol officer","patrolperson","patrol ship","patrol van","patrol vehicle","patrol wagon","patrolwoman","saturation patrol","senior patrol leader","Sharia patrol","shore patrol","ski patrol","squadrol"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patrol#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6b6c6db23a329e440e","definition":"To go the rounds of, as a sentry, guard, or policeman","example":"to patrol a frontier","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["border patrol","combat air patrol","dawn pat